{"seconds": 252.8, "exit": 0, "final": "After 4. Rf6+ Ke4, White has a dominating position and Black's position collapses. The main point: **Nxe6** is the killing blow because it wins a pawn with a devastating fork, and after Black's forced recapture Nxe6, White continues hxg6+ with an overwhelming attack that forces the Black king into the center where it perishes.\n\n**Best move:** Nxe6\n\n**Main line:** Nxe6 Nxe6 hxg6+ Kxg6 Rh6+ Kf5 Rf6+ Ke4\n\n**Motif:** Fork (the knight attacks two pieces: Nc7 and Rg7)\n\n**Explanation (coaching note):**\nLook for pieces that are attacked but defended only once. Here, e6 is defended only by the Ne7. When you capture with Nxe6, you fork both the Ne7 and the distant Rg7\u2014Black must recapture, losing control. Then hxg6+ drives the king forward into White's waiting rooks. The lesson: a pawn \"only defended once\" is a magnet for tactics; attacking it forces your opponent's hand.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nxe6\", \"line\": [\"Nxe6\", \"Nxe6\", \"hxg6+\", \"Kxg6\", \"Rh6+\", \"Kf5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42", "square": "f7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42", "square": "g6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/1rn1n1r1/2p1p1pk/p1PpP1NP/Pp1P1Pp1/1P6/1K5R/7R w - - 1 42", "move": "Nf7+"}}, 